SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

This repository ships a mix of vendored upstream code and project-local
glue. Each file's own SPDX header and copyright lines are authoritative;
this file is an overview, not a license re-grant.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Vendored upstream sources (vendor/openeuler/)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Sourced verbatim from the OpenEuler kernel
(https://gitee.com/openeuler/kernel, branch OLK-6.6).

Two distinct copyright groups exist within vendor/openeuler/:

  1. Files originally authored by Huawei for OpenEuler — every file
     under vendor/openeuler/fs/nfs/enfs/, the
     vendor/openeuler/fs/nfs/enfs_adapter.{c,h} pair, and the
     sunrpc_enfs_adapter sources/header. These carry an explicit
     "Copyright (c) Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd." line and are
     licensed GPL-2.0-only.

  2. Stock Linux kernel files that OpenEuler patches but that retain
     their original kernel-author copyrights — fs/nfs/{super.c,
     fs_context.c, nfs3xdr.c, internal.h, Kconfig, Makefile},
     net/sunrpc/{clnt.c, xprt.c, Kconfig, Makefile} and several
     headers under include/linux/. The named copyright holders are the
     original Linux NFS / SunRPC subsystem contributors (Rick Sladkey,
     David Howells, Olaf Kirch, and others — see each file). These are
     GPL-2.0-only as inherited from the Linux kernel.

Do not modify SPDX or copyright headers in any vendor/openeuler/ file.

The pinned upstream commit is recorded in
vendor/openeuler/UPSTREAM-REVISION.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Vendored upstream sources (vendor/ubuntu-7.0/)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Sourced verbatim from the Ubuntu 26.04 LTS kernel source package
linux_7.0.0-14.14 (the 14 stock Linux files that enfs needs to patch).
These are vendored under GPL-2.0-only and each retains its original
SPDX-License-Identifier and Linux kernel-author copyright header
verbatim — Rick Sladkey, David Howells, Olaf Kirch and the wider
Linux NFS / SunRPC subsystem contributors. Per-file copyrights are
preserved exactly; this overview does not re-grant or amend them.

Do not modify SPDX or copyright headers in any vendor/ubuntu-7.0/
file.

The pinned upstream package (Ubuntu kernel package and ABI) is
recorded in vendor/ubuntu-7.0/UPSTREAM-REVISION
(currently linux_7.0.0-14.14). The patches we apply on top live in
patches/ubuntu-7.0/ and are listed by patches/ubuntu-7.0/series.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Project glue (everything outside vendor/openeuler/ and vendor/ubuntu-7.0/)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Makefiles, Kbuild, dkms.conf.in, compat/, scripts/, debian/, docs/,
patches/series, patches/ubuntu-7.0/*.patch, README, this file, etc.
are written for this DKMS port and licensed GPL-2.0-only by enfs-dkms
contributors. They are intentionally compatible with the kernel
modules they produce.

debian/copyright contains file-glob-specific stanzas matching what is
actually in each vendored file's header.

